    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d591">

                <pb facs="0889" n="879" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg879"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Major General S. L. Howard, U. S. M. C., to the
                        Commander of the Seventh Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Cooke</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tientsin</hi>
                        </placeName>] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1946-10-23">23 October
                            1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>220628Z. Executive Headquarters does not wish to send team into Tangku area for
                    rescue of two Marines. Request for rescue has been addressed to both Nationalist
                    and Communist representatives at Executive Hqs. Nationalist Headquarters state
                    they have initiated action. Communist Hqs. state they will forward the request
                    to Yenan.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
